WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.270
<b>Silver General</b>

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.440
You play shogi, too?

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.450
Sort of. Just for fun, though.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.600
Tsume shogi?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.330
<b>Bishop</b>

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.510
Mornin'!

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.180
What're you playing this boring game for?

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.390
Shogi is not boring.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.410
It's no game, either.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.310
I'm... sorry.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.710
<b>ETOTAMA</b>

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:30.750
<b>Episode 9: The Beauty of Flowers, 
Bird Steps, and Moon</b>

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:30.030
I told you, I won't let a stupid cat like you

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.790
have your way all the time, stupid cat!

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.180
Don't call me stupid!

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.310
What's wrong with calling 
a stupid cat "stupid"?

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.630
Just get out of here!

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.740
I won't! I'm going to join the—

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:40.920
The zodiac doesn't need a stupid cat!

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.490
You'll never be part of it!

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:44.630
The ETM12 rules say if I get

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.520
all twelve of your Sol/Lull Seals, I can!

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.140
Oh? Then how many do you have now?

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.140
Mo-tan, Usa-tan, Mei-tan, Shima-tan,

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.230
Key, Inu, Shar-tan, and Uma-tan!

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.530
You're still missing four.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.530
It'll be fine!

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:01.790
You think you can beat Chu-tan?

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.580
The strongest of the Eto-shin?

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.570
How? Do you have a plan?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.120
Do you have the confidence?  
Do you have any basis to back that up?

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:11.750
T-Takeru...

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.640
Look how dirty it is now...

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.710
Um... Takeru-han?

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.970
Chu-tan aside, you'll never defeat me.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.890
I can beat you! Choose your method 
of battle right now, Piyo-tan!

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.050
Shogi.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.230
Okay! Let's get the Sol/Lull Seal battle—

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.240
Don't underestimate shogi.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.190
Shogi is the universe.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.300
Uh...

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:43.440
Okay, anyway, the Sol/Lull Seal battle—

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:43.950
I'm saying...

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.660
Wait, Nya-tan.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.580
Why?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.980
You don't know anything about shogi yet.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.010
You should first play a casual game

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.540
with Piyo-tan, unbound by rules.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.920
<b>King</b>

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.590
I just put these pieces 
of wood on the board?

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:13.440
Now, let us begin, Nya-tan-san.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.470
Huh?! Who are you now?!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.940
<b>Eto Rank
Master Piyo</b>

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.940
Eto rank: Master Piyo.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:19.610
Who's that?!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.260
The game between Master Piyo and

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:25.320
Nya-tan will now begin.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.050
Wait a moment. The handicap...

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.700
You're right. She'll need a handicap.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:32.960
<b>Pawn</b>

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:38.380
<b>Naked King</b>

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.310
Naked king and three pawns.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:38.380
<b>Three Pawns</b>

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.080
Let us play.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.380
We'll play, all right!

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.630
<b>King</b>

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.630
<b>Promoted Pawn</b>

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:40.630
Check.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.580
Nya-tan has lost this game.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.390
What?

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.460
Why? How did I lose?

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.340
When your king is cornered, you lose.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.470
This is not worth my time.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.560
You can never defeat me with 
that childish mentality.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.000
Don't lecture me like some bigshot 
over a dumb game like shogi!

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:03.800
Nya-tan, shogi is not a "dumb game."

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.070
Shogi is the universe.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.220
Sorry, Takeru, you keep saying that,

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.990
but I have no idea what it means.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.250
Indeed...

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.620
Shogi is the universe.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.960
Shogi is numbers, flow, and logic.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.190
Within that framework, 
energy streams outward,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.500
never breaking, always upholding the rules.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.830
Just like the universe,

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.880
still expanding infinitely even now.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.700
Shogi is body, mind, and existence itself.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.460
It is all living things in 
this world materialized.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.960
It is born and grows within us,

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:46.400
sometimes changing as we 
battle with ourselves.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.000
It is eternal.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.090
It only makes sense to liken such a thing to

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.600
the universe that gave our 
world its beginning.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.120
Um, um...

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.880
Okay, just take three steps 
and forget everythi—

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.560
You can't pretend it never happened

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.880
just because it's turned into a pain.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.130
I'll make you see that no matter 
what cool things you say,

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.520
you'll forget it instantly anyway!

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:09.690
I know that!

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.190
Once I take three steps, I forget.

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:15.330
I forget almost everything.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.260
But as is the nature of the rooster clan,

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.740
only negative emotions remain in me forever,

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.020
piling higher and higher.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.570
<b>King</b>

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.570
<b>Promoted Pawn</b>

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.370
When I was about to be engulfed 
by those negative emotions,

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.570
only shogi could save me.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:30.470
While playing shogi, I can become empty.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.410
By playing shogi, I can be myself.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.340
I understand how you feel.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.080
Seriously?!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:41.880
point

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.780
Play me one more time!

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:44.750
I refuse.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.630
As you are now, you can 
only play useless shogi.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:54.580
Takeru! Train me in how to play shogi!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.430
<b>Menacing</b>

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.430
I won't lose to that chicken who 
falls flat off the starting line!

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.800
Interesting.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.310
Then, when your training is 
complete, I'll play you again.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.320
With our Sol/Lull Seals 
on the line this time.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.030
All right! I'll be waiting!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.680
Takeru, train me!

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.120
Nya-tan, you already know how 
each piece moves, right?

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.250
Of course I do! Perfectly!

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.470
That's a huge shogi board!

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:27.530
I made it with my Sol/Lull.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.800
It's my special Shogi 
Master Training Board.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.470
Okay, start with the pawn!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.340
<b>Pawn</b>

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:33.340
Pawn!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.260
Pawn, pawn...

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.190
The pawn can only move forward 
one space at a time!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.210
Scary...

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.490
Making her learn shogi physically, huh?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.860
That shogi board is the 
materialization of what happens

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.190
when Takeru-san gets serious,  
expressed through the power of Eto-shin.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.530
<b>Rook</b>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.530
Next, the rook!

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.030
Hi-meow!

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.840
The rook can only move up, 
down, left, or right!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.540
<b>Bishop</b>

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.450
Hot!

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.540
The bishop can move any number 
of spaces diagonally!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:07.540
<b>Silver General</b>

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:05.160
Hot again!

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:07.240
Silver can only move one space 
forward or diagonally!

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.800
<b>Gold General</b>

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:10.970
Uri!

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.800
Gold can move one space in any 
direction but diagonally backwards!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.680
<b>Knight</b>

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.990
Horse!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:16.010
The knight moves two spaces forward, 
then one space to either left or right!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:20.430
<b>Lance</b>

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.430
<b>Eek!</b>

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:18.850
Cow!

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.800
The lance moves straight ahead!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.900
<b>Eek!</b>

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.900
By the way, kings can move 
one space in any direction!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.320
<b>Pant Pant</b>

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.320
Shogi... is terrifying...

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.400
<b>Pant Pant</b>

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.400
Have you learned how the pieces move now?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.810
She's totally learned it.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.240
In the form of trauma.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.500
So this training is to make 
her learn it physically

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.630
as well as to train her mentally, then?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:44.790
Get a little stronger now 
while ya can, Nya-tan.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:46.580
That's it for today!

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.390
All right, let's begin today's training.

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.130
Okay!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.330
Today, we'll use Dora-tan's special

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:59.340
Shogi Master Training Screen Door Board

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:01.230
to play blindfolded shogi.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:02.980
Blindfolded shogi?

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.620
You play shogi in your head.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.170
Picture the shogi board, imagine your hand,

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:10.640
and predict the opponent's moves.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:11.820
I can't do that!

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.650
If you can't do this, 
you can never beat Piyo-tan.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.580
Okay, fine! I'll do it!

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.080
7-6, pawn!

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.540
Then I'll...

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.040
Where? Where?!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.600
That's dangerous!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.170
That was 8-4, pawn.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:34.030
You need to predict where I'll move 
and dodge it, or you'll be stabbed.

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:34.800
Yep, yep!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.110
Are you serious?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:37.300
In that case...

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.050
6-8, silver!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.850
6-2, silver!

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.180
That one might have been easy to predict.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.050
5-6, pawn!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.440
That was 5-4, pawn!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:56.490
Hey, you boar!

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.720
I just added a little spice to it.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.490
Don't spice it up without warning!

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.660
And you know, I can't 
think calmly like this!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.680
You won't always be in situations 
where you can think calmly!

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.160
Come on! We're not stopping 
until the sun goes down!

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.000
Nya-tan, you can do it!

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.000
<b>
Even a Cat Can Understand! 

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:18.160
The quickest way to learn how to play shogi

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.280
is to memorize all the shogi proverbs.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.970
<b>Certain Victory</b>

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.970
<b>Book of Shogi Proverbs</b>

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.970
There are so many complicated words...

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.150
The strategies themselves are often 
expressed in these proverbs.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:30.040
So you should...

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.390
I think that's all for today.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:45.040
<b>[Zodiac Precepts ~Article 11: "Promotion"] 
If an Eto-musume collects Sol/Lull Seals from all of the Eto-shin, 
she will be promoted to Eto-shin. The newly-promoted Eto-shin 
earns the right to demote one Eto-shin to Eto-musume.</b>

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:50.080
<b>[Zodiac Precepts ~Article 12: "Precepts"] 
The Zodiac Precepts protect the chaste souls of the Eto 
and govern the Eto-shin Selection Festival (ETM12). 
Any Eto-musume who violates these Precepts 
will be judged by the Conference of Gods.</b>

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.370
Here I come!

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.240
Don't give up!

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.130
Hold on to the powerful 
desire to play shogi!

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.770
Nya-tan! With a half-hearted attitude,

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.640
you can't even touch a shogi board!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.150
One more time! Here I come!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.150
You're not feeling it enough!

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.630
I won't lose...

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.410
I won't lose!

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.730
3-4, pawn!

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.700
6-6, pawn!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.200
4-2, silver!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.080
5-8, silver, right!

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.800
<b>Book of Shogi Proverbs</b>

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.800
<b>Amazing!</b>

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.290
3-2, gold!

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:53.370
4-1, king!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.610
5-3, gold!

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.970
<b>King</b>

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:25.470
<b>Please take one</b>

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:32.770
Let's go.

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.450
Yeah!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.770
First off, 2-6, pawn!

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:39.720
3-4, pawn!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:41.610
2-5, pawn!

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.430
3-3, bishop!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.720
<i>I can tell... I can tell!</i>

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.450
7-6, pawn!

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:49.970
<i>The fight's on!</i>

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:59.210
Your move is 2-2, silver.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.780
Well done, Nya-tan!

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.260
You read my moves perfectly!

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.700
Shogi is all about getting 
into your opponent's head.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.830
Knowing what your opponent is thinking,

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:15.580
and how you should fight them...

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.350
To always have an eye on the future.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:19.230
That's how you read their moves.

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.820
Let's play a game tonight.

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:22.920
Okay.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.630
We've been totally left behind, haven't we?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:28.650
Yeah.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.150
This is...

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.450
You've done well to come this far.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.660
Takeru, shogi is really fun.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.090
Nya-tan.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.670
I was playing

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.210
against myself just now.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.670
Yes... That's why shogi is the universe.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:28.010
Your face looks much better,

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.340
Nya-tan.

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:32.890
Thank you for the game.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.550
Will this really be okay?

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:36.870
Will what be okay?

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.480
This anime.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.480
Oh, she's here!

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:47.740
It looks like you've made progress.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.360
It's time to battle!

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.300
Then let's start the game!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:55.620
<b>Approved</b>

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.590
Etotama! Sol/Lull Charge!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:57.830
<b>Rooster                           Cat</b>

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.600
Cat Eto-musume, Nya-tan!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:21.640
Rooster Eto-musume, Piyo-tan!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:50.730
Today, I am me, but I am not me.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.390
My moves are the moves of motionlessness.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.050
A pawn is worth a thousand golds.

00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:59.580
The battle begins with a pawn's sacrifice.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.900
Um...

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.360
What are they talking about?

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:07.340
Nya-tan said, "If you get careless because

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.740
you think I'm a lower rank, you'll lose."

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:13.530
And Piyo-tan said, 
"That confidence just because

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.830
you can play shogi a little now

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.620
is what will bring about your defeat."

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.830
Oh...

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.900
They're having a conversation 
with shogi proverbs.

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.620
This has gotten pretty wild.

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:24.670
They're starting.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:32.130
Nekodamashi?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.760
<b>Nekodamashi</b>

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.570
That's a rather unusual move to start with.

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:40.270
No, the nekodamashi isn't 
a tricky move at all.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.810
The patterns of moves that could 
begin here are infinite.

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:48.360
A moment ago, you said your 
moves are motionless.

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:51.360
My moves are nomadic.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:54.740
I allow them to dance as 
freely as they wish.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:59.370
<i>Nya-tan, your moves are building up a flow!</i>

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.540
This is good! Nya-tan has the advantage!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.590
I had thought this might be

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:22.710
an interesting game, but...

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:28.810
A torisashi now?!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:28.810
<b>Torisashi</b>

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.340
What happened?

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.530
I have no idea!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:35.900
That one move by Piyo-tan just 
turned the tide of this game.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:36.910
What?!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.410
How? What's going on?

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.380
You were drifting about within

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.160
the flow that I created.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.790
You thought you had arrived 
on the other side,

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:13.910
but you were still adrift in the 
midst of this great river.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.570
Is Nya-tan gonna lose?

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.240
It'll be really difficult to get 
out of her current position.

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:23.540
Honestly, in the same position, 
I'd have no plan.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.580
What?!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.910
Well, I dunno what's goin' on,

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:30.120
but this is turnin' into 
one intense battle.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.540
Yes, this isn't like Nya-tan at all.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.950
<i>I might have been suppressing what's</i>

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:38.720
<i>great about Nya-tan...</i>

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.930
<i>Nya-tan! There's a saying 
I haven't taught you yet!</i>

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:45.570
If you learn this proverb too soon,

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:48.320
you can never learn to play shogi properly.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.620
That's why I didn't tell you.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:51.460
But...

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.770
<i>You're ready now!</i>

00:18:55.230 --> 00:19:08.330
<b>A Master</b>

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.190
A master needs no patterns!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:08.330
<b>Needs No Patterns</b>

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.200
A shogi master doesn't rely 
on standard patterns alone,

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:05.200
but reads and uses many 
unique moves to win!

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.690
That's what the proverb means.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:11.450
A master needs no patterns...

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.870
That's right!

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:21.060
<i>To walk the magnificent path of the 
past that is standard patterns,</i>

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:26.070
<i>striving for one's own desired 
destination at its end...</i>

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.330
<i>Is this... a piece of me?</i>

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.660
I felt like

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:41.570
I was on the verge of 
remembering something...

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:45.380
I finally understand!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.110
Shogi is the universe!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.750
I'll embrace that universe

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.830
and play shogi my way!

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:02.930
Cat clan secret technique:

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.350
<b>Nekojarashi</b>

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:05.350
Nekojarashi!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.510
What?

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.730
What is that?

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.870
I've lost.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.270
Thank you for the game.

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.790
Sh-She won...

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.800
Nya-tan won!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.320
All right!

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.710
M-My feet...

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.180
Th-They're numb...

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.180
<b>Ache            Ache</b>

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.180
<b>Rooster</b>

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:54.110
It hurts! It hurts! It really hurts!

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.570
What is this?! I hate shogi!

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:58.190
It's boring! It's no fun at all!

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.940
I've had enough! I'll never play it again!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:03.400
I'm hungry! I'm having yakiniku 
to celebrate my victory!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:05.860
<b>Step</b>

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:06.570
<b>Steps</b>

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.280
<b>Steps</b>

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:16.490
Hey! Why do you have my Sol/Lull Seal?!

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:18.660
I won it from you in battle!

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.070
What? That's impossible! Don't lie!

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:23.720
I'm not lying! I put up a really good fight!

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:24.830
Good grief...

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.070
Stop lying, you stupid cat!

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:25.940
What'd you say, stupid?!

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.520
I'm gonna go get Takeru!

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:39.020
She turned back into the 
old Nya-tan in no time.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.590
Okay!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.070
I wanted to play one more game with her...

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.890
Takeru, we're ready to start 
cooking the yakiniku!

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:46.470
Okay, I'll be right there.

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:56.900
Okay, now let's go have yakiniku!

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:00.130
Meat! Meat! Meat!

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:02.690
Nya-tan needs no patterns.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:47.150
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.930
Here's the fortune for those born 
in the year of the rooster.

00:23:37.930 --> 00:23:40.140
Whatever you do, don't hang 
around any stupid cats.

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:41.080
That is al—

00:23:42.560 --> 00:23:45.610
Er... Huh? What was I talking about?

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.150
You took three steps.

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:49.500
Next time: Eternal Pervert.

00:23:47.150 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Eternal Pervert</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Remember this until next week!</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Illustration: Sasaki Mikoi</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>You... 
Stupid cat!!!</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Rooster</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:54.020
<b>Cheep Cheep</b>
